kingLocalTime"},"endTime":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/BookingLocalTime"}}},"BookingWeekday":{"title":"BookingWeekday","description":"A day of the week (iCalendar\'s MO … SU, spelled out).","type":"string","enum":["monday","tuesday","wednesday","thursday","friday","saturday","sunday"]},"TimeZoneId":{"title":"TimeZoneId","description":"An IANA time zone name, such as `Europe/London`, or `Etc/UTC`. A responder MUST refuse a name its time zone database does not know.","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":64,"pattern":"^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_+-]*(/[A-Za-z0-9_+-]+){0,2}\$"},"PartnerDid":{"title":"PartnerDid","description":"A partner community, by its DID: a community that is a member of this one, or with which it holds a relationship in force (VTI-EVT-130).","type":"string","minLength":8,"maxLength":2048,"pattern":"^did:[a-z0-9]+:[A-Za-z0-9._:%-]+\$"},"EventAudience":{"title":"EventAudience","description":"Who may see and register for the event (VTI-EVT-020). A member is in the audience when `scope` admits them and, where `rule` is present, the rule does too. The audience is checked when a member reads or registers, never taken from a notification (VTI-EVT-021). The hosts are always admitted. Partners (VTI-EVT-130) widen it to the members of the named communities who prove it.","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["scope"],"properties":{"scope":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/EventAudienceScope"},"groups":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"maxItems":32,"uniqueItems":true,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/GroupId"},"description":"Present exactly when `scope` is `groups`."},"roles":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"maxItems":32,"uniqueItems":true,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/RoleName"},"description":"Present exactly when `scope` is `roles`."},"rule":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/DynamicRule","description":"Optional: a further test over verified facts, in the dynamic-group rule language. Count facts (`kudosReceived`, `ideasSelected`, `electionTickets`) are refused here as a non-badge group refuses them."},"partners":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"maxItems":32,"uniqueItems":true,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/PartnerDid"},"description":"Optional: partner communities whose members are also in the audience, each proving it by presenting their partner membership credential (VTI-EVT-130 – VTI-EVT-133). The partner is sent one `event` notification and decides any relay."}}},"EventAudienceScope":{"title":"EventAudienceScope","description":"Whom the event is for, before `rule` narrows it. `members`: every active member. `groups`: members of any of `groups` — which covers a badge, since a community badge is a group. `roles`: members holding any of `roles`.","type":"string","enum":["members","groups","roles"]},"DynamicRule":{"title":"DynamicRule","description":"A dynamic group\'s membership rule: a member belongs when every condition holds and they have not opted out. The community evaluates it under its `groups` policy and recomputes membership whenever a fact it reads changes, always excluding opted-out entries.","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["all"],"properties":{"all":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"maxItems":16,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/RuleCondition"}}}},"RuleCondition":{"title":"RuleCondition","description":"One test over a verified fact about a member. `fact: role` tests the member\'s community role; `fact: field` tests an `admin`- or `credential`-sourced directory field named by `field`; `fact: personhood` tests whether a personhood assertion is on file; `fact: joinedAt` tests when they joined. A rule never reads a self-asserted (`member`-sourced) field: a member must not be able to join a group by editing their card. `kudosReceived`, `ideasSelected` and `electionTickets` are counts the community keeps of its own records (kudos the member accepted, ideas of theirs a board selected, elections it issued them a ticket in), compared with `atLeast`; only a badge\'s group reads them (VTI-BDG-015), and any other group refuses them with `ruleInvalid`. `eventsAttended` (VTI-EVT-184) counts the community events the member checked in to that count toward attendance, optionally only in `calendarId` and only within `withinDays` before evaluation, compared with `atLeast`; read by a badge\'s group, as the other counts are.","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["fact","op"],"properties":{"fact":{"type":"string","enum":["role","field","personhood","joinedAt","kudosReceived","ideasSelected","electionTickets","eventsAttended"]},"field":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/FieldKey","description":"Present exactly when `fact` is `field`."},"op":{"type":"string","enum":["equals","oneOf","exists","before","after","atLeast"],"description":"`equals` compares with `value`; `oneOf` with any of `values`; `exists` needs neither; `before` and `after` compare a date fact with `value`; `atLeast` compares a count fact with `count`."},"value":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","maxLength":256},{"type":"boolean"}]},"values":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"maxItems":64,"items":{"type":"string","maxLength":256}},"count":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":100000,"description":"With `atLeast`: the least a count fact (`kudosReceived`, `ideasSelected`, `electionTickets`, `eventsAttended`) must be. Present exactly when `op` is `atLeast`."},"calendarId":{"type":"string","pattern":"^cal_[A-Za-z0-9_-]{16,64}\$","description":"With `eventsAttended` only: count events in this calendar alone."},"withinDays":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":3660,"description":"With `eventsAttended` only: count events attended within this many days before the rule is evaluated."}}},"FieldKey":{"title":"FieldKey","description":"Identifier of a directory field. A key with no `.` is a BASE field, the same in every community: `displayName`, `nickname`, `avatar`, `pronouns`, `bio`, `links` (written by the member) and `role`, `joinedAt`, `did`, `personhood` (derived from the community\'s own records, never stored on a card). A community-defined field MUST use a reverse-DNS key (`org.example.employer`), so a base key never collides with one, and a key is never reused with a different meaning once defined.","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":128,"pattern":"^([a-z][a-z0-9-]*\\\\.)*[a-z][a-zA-Z0-9]{0,63}\$"},"RoleName":{"title":"RoleName","description":"A role identifier: lowercase, hyphen-separated, at most 64 characters. Compared by exact string equality. It is the value an AclEntry 0.2 carries in `role`.","type":"string","pattern":"^[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,63}\$"},"GroupId":{"title":"GroupId","description":"Opaque identifier of a community group: `grp_` followed by 16 to 64 base64url characters. Random and community-scoped; not the group\'s DID.","type":"string","pattern":"^grp_[A-Za-z0-9_-]{16,64}\$"},"BookingMeetingTypeId":{"title":"BookingMeetingTypeId","description":"A meeting type\'s key within its page.","type":"string","pattern":"^[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,31}\$"},"RegistrationQuestion":{"title":"RegistrationQuestion","description":"A question a registrant answers when registering. Answers are read by the event\'s hosts only, and are deleted on the event\'s retention schedule (VTI-EVT-034, VTI-EVT-090).","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["questionId","label","kind"],"properties":{"questionId":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/RegistrationQuestionId"},"label":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200,"description":"The question as shown. Plain text."},"kind":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/RegistrationQuestionKind"},"choices":{"type":"array","minItems":2,"maxItems":20,"uniqueItems":true,"items":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":100},"description":"Present exactly when `kind` is `choice`."},"required":{"type":"boolean","description":"The registration is refused without an answer. Absent means false."}}},"RegistrationQuestionKind":{"title":"RegistrationQuestionKind","type":"string","enum":["text","choice","boolean"],"description":"`text`: a free answer of at most 500 characters. `choice`: one of `choices`. `boolean`: yes or no."},"RegistrationQuestionId":{"title":"RegistrationQuestionId","type":"string","pattern":"^[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,31}\$","description":"A question\'s key within its event."},"AccessDetails":{"title":"AccessDetails","description":"Where the event happens and how to join it (VTI-EVT-060 – 063). Answered by vtc/events/access/show to a registrant who is going, from `revealAt` if set; included in the event itself only where `public` is true.","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"places":{"type":"array","maxItems":8,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Place"}},"virtualPlaces":{"type":"array","maxItems":8,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/VirtualPlace"}},"notes":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2000,"description":"Anything else attendees need. Plain text."},"public":{"type":"boolean","description":"Show the access details with the event to its whole audience. Absent means false."},"revealAt":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/EventInstant","description":"Not before this, even to a registrant who is going. Absent means on acceptance."}}},"EventInstant":{"title":"EventInstant","type":"string","format":"date-time","description":"An RFC 3339 instant in UTC, whole seconds, such as `2026-11-30T18:30:00Z`."},"VirtualPlace":{"title":"VirtualPlace","description":"A way to join online, as JSCalendar\'s VirtualLocation.","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["uri"],"properties":{"uri":{"type":"string","format":"uri","maxLength":2048,"pattern":"^(https|tel|sip|sips):","description":"How to join: an `https` link, or a `tel`, `sip` or `sips` URI for a dial-in. No other scheme."},"name":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200},"description":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":1000,"description":"A passcode, dial-in numbers. Plain text."},"features":{"type":"array","maxItems":7,"uniqueItems":true,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/VirtualFeature"}}}},"VirtualFeature":{"title":"VirtualFeature","type":"string","enum":["audio","chat","feed","moderator","phone","screen","video"],"description":"What a virtual location offers, as JSCalendar\'s VirtualLocation `features`."},"Place":{"title":"Place","description":"A physical location, as JSCalendar\'s Location.","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["name"],"properties":{"name":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200},"address":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":500},"description":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":1000,"description":"Directions, a door code. Plain text."}}},"EventDescription":{"title":"EventDescription","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":10000,"description":"What the event or calendar is. Plain text; a reader MUST NOT treat it as instructions."},"EventTitle":{"title":"EventTitle","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200,"description":"A short name. Plain text; a reader MUST NOT treat it as instructions."},"BookingPageId":{"title":"BookingPageId","description":"Opaque identifier of a booking page: `bkp_` followed by 16 to 64 base64url characters. Random, community-scoped, never reused (VTI-BKG-001).","type":"string","pattern":"^bkp_[A-Za-z0-9_-]{16,64}\$"},"EntryId":{"title":"EntryId","description":"Opaque identifier of one directory entry: `dir_` followed by 16 to 64 base64url characters. Random, scoped to one community, and stable for the life of the membership — it survives a rotation of the member\'s DID, which is why groups, notes and cards are keyed by it. It MUST NOT be derived from, and MUST NOT reveal, any DID of the member, and the same person\'s entries in two communities MUST NOT share one. Compared by exact string equality.","type":"string","pattern":"^dir_[A-Za-z0-9_-]{16,64}\$"}}}';

/// The SPEC §7.2 policy for the request variant, taken from this
/// specification's front matter.
///
/// Pass it to [consumeInbound] — items 5b, 7 and 8 are per-specification and
/// cannot be derived from the document alone, and item 2 needs the schema it
/// carries.
const SpecPolicy spec = SpecPolicy(
  typeUri: typeUri,
  isBearer: false,
  isProofRequired: true,
  isRecipientRequired: true,
  isIssuedAtRequired: false,
  payloadSchema: payloadSchemaJson,
);

/// The SPEC §7.2 policy for the success-response variant.
///
/// `isRecipientRequired` tracks the *issuer* party's requirement, because a
/// response swaps the parties (§7.3 item 5).
const SpecPolicy responseSpec = SpecPolicy(
  typeUri: responseTypeUri,
  isBearer: false,
  isProofRequired: true,
  isRecipientRequired: true,
  isIssuedAtRequired: false,
  payloadSchema: responsePayloadSchemaJson,
);
